// Jina Search REST (s.jina.ai): the `jina` provider of the web_search chain.
//
// Search only. Jina Reader (r.jina.ai), which fetches and converts one page,
// is not declared: page reading is out of scope for web_search.
//
// Wire contract pinned from Jina's own documentation (read 2026-10-20):
// - the search operation of Jina's published OpenAPI document,
//   https://s.jina.ai/openapi.json (path /{q}, its parameters, headers,
//   content types and listed responses);
// - the Search section and rate-limit table of the Reader page,
//   https://jina.ai/reader/#search and https://jina.ai/reader/#rate-limit;
// - the README and search source of Jina's open-source server,
//   https://github.com/jina-ai/reader (README.md, src/api/searcher.ts,
//   src/services/serp/serper.ts), for the headers the OpenAPI omits.
//
// - method and path: GET https://s.jina.ai/<url-encoded query>; the OpenAPI
//   path is /{q}. The query is sent as that whole path segment, fully
//   percent-encoded (the manifest marks `q` a free-text path parameter, so
//   a "/" in a query is sent as %2F rather than refused, and diagnostics
//   print "/{q}", never the query). Jina also documents ?q= and POST forms;
//   neither is used;
// - auth: "Authorization: Bearer jina_...", so the key goes in
//   `Authorization` with the `Bearer ` prefix. The OpenAPI says search
//   requires a key, and the rate-limit table marks keyless search blocked.
//   The connection is bound to the vault credential `apikey:jina`; plexus
//   reads it by name at dispatch and never stores it;
// - request fields used: `count` (query parameter, 0 to 20 in the OpenAPI;
//   1 to 20 is sent), and one domain in the `X-Site` header (the server
//   source reads `x-site` and turns it into a site: filter). JSON output
//   comes from `Accept: application/json`, which the REST transport sends on
//   every request. `X-Respond-With: no-content` is sent on every request as
//   a reviewed constant: the server source then returns search listings
//   without crawling each result page, which web_search never reads. The
//   OpenAPI also documents num, page, gl, hl, location, engine/provider and
//   crawler headers (X-Engine, X-Retain-Images and others); none are sent
//   and they are not in the reviewed schema;
// - reply: {code, status, data, meta}, where `data` is an array of results
//   with `title`, `url`, `description` and, when page content is fetched,
//   `content`; the OpenAPI result schema names a publication date
//   `publishedTime`, and the server's SERP results name it `date`;
// - errors: the OpenAPI lists 400, 401, 402, 403, 422, 429, 500 and 503,
//   with an error object of `code`, `status`, `message` and an optional
//   `readableMessage`. No Retry-After header is documented;
// - limits: no query-length limit is documented (the Reader page says
//   none); the rate-limit table gives s.jina.ai 100 requests per minute for
//   free and paid keys and 1,000 for premium keys, tracked per key.
//
// Differences from the provider facts the web_search chain design started from
// (GET https://s.jina.ai/<url-encoded query>; Bearer auth; count, max 20;
// one domain via X-Site; title, url, description or content):
// - none in method, path, auth, count or the result fields named there;
// - X-Site is not in the OpenAPI document; it is read by Jina's server source
//   and shown in its README. The source would also split a comma-separated
//   list into several sites, but the design allows one domain, so the
//   backend declares a maximum of one and two or more domains skip Jina;
// - X-Respond-With: no-content is sent in addition, from the server source;
//   it is not in the OpenAPI list of response formats. If Jina ignored it,
//   the reply would only carry extra `content`, and `description` would
//   still be read first;
// - recency: Jina documents no date filter, so a search with recency skips
//   Jina for capability instead of returning results of any age;
// - query length: none is documented, so the tool's own 500-character limit
//   applies;
// - a publication date is reported from `date` or `publishedTime` when it is
//   a parseable date, and dropped otherwise;
// - empty results: Jina's search source answers a search that found nothing
//   with an error that the OpenAPI lists as 422, not with an empty `data`.
//   The chain treats every 400 and 422 as a rejected request without reading
//   the body, so such a search is refused as web_search_request_rejected and
//   is not retried on the next provider. A 200 with an empty `data` array is
//   served as an empty result;
// - classification needs no Jina-specific rule: 401 is a credential failure,
//   402 a quota skip with the one-hour cooldown, 429 throttled for 60
//   seconds (no Retry-After is documented), 403 another client error and
//   500 and 503 server errors, all three unavailable for 60 seconds.
//
// The search action is read-risk and has no side effects, so a retry is safe.
{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "key": "jina_rest",
  "name": "Jina Search (REST)",
  "description": "Web search over Jina's Search API (s.jina.ai), as a provider for web_search.",
  "reuse_path": "openapi_shim",
  "reuse_rationale": "Documented REST API with a published OpenAPI spec and static API-key bearer auth; a search mutates no vendor-side state, so it maps to a read grant.",
  "tier": "S1",
  "transport": {
    "kind": "rest_api",
    "url": "https://s.jina.ai"
  },
  "auth": {
    "mode": "api_key"
  },
  "credential_bindings": [
    {
      "ref_role": "api_key",
      "placement": "header",
      "key": "Authorization",
      "prefix": "Bearer ",
      "required": true
    }
  ],
  "resource_filters": {
    "required": [],
    "optional": [],
    "write_enabling": []
  },
  "actions_baseline": [
    {
      "name": "search",
      "risk": "read",
      "http": {
        "method": "GET",
        "path": "/{q}",
        "parameters": "query",
        "text_path_parameters": ["q"],
        "header_parameters": {
          "site": "X-Site",
          "respond_with": "X-Respond-With"
        },
        "request_constants": {
          "respond_with": "no-content"
        },
        "args_schema": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "q": { "type": "string", "minLength": 1, "maxLength": 500 },
            "count": { "type": "integer", "minimum": 1, "maximum": 20 },
            "site": { "type": "string", "minLength": 1, "maxLength": 253 }
          },
          "required": ["q"],
          "additionalProperties": false
        }
      }
    }
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "ask_first_risk": ["write", "destructive"],
    "rate_limit": { "calls_per_min": 30 }
  },
  "availability": "ga"
}
